==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|tīd}}, {{IPA|en|/taɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-tied.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|[tʰaːd]|a=Southern US,AAVE}}
* {{IPA|en|[tʰɑe̯d]|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{homophones|en|tide}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪd|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[closely|Closely]] [[associated#Adjective|associated]] or [[connected#Adjective|connected]].
#: {{ux|en|As a couple, they are strongly '''tied''' to one another.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Berliner Discusses ' Problem|work=Daily Collegian|location=State College, PA|date=October 19, 1961|passage=It is financially too '''tied''' to West Germany to exist by itself, he explained .}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Why Cut Rates Again When Recovery Is Near?|work=Hartford (CT) Courant|date=June 24, 2003|passage=But this time -- because of the rare and dangerous threat of widespread price declines -- the anticipated rate cut is even more '''tied''' to mental mechanics.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Obama: Clinton too '''tied''' to DC insiders|work=Myrtle Beach (NC) Sun News|date=March 27, 2008|passage=Sen. Barack Obama said Wednesday that his chief rival, Sen. Hillary Clinton, was too closely '''tied''' to the Washington status quo to bring about change.}}
# [[restricted#Adjective|Restricted]].
# [[conditional#Adjective|Conditional]] on other [[agreement]]s being [[uphold|upheld]].
# {{lb|en|liquor trade}} Of a [[public house]], bar, etc., obliged to sell [[beer]] from only one [[brewery]], or [[alcoholic]] drinks from one [[pubco]].
# {{lb|en|sports|or|games}} That resulted in a [[tie]].
# Provided for use by an employer for as long as one is employed, often with restrictions on the conditions of use.
# {{lb|en|archeology}} Having walls that are connected in a few places by a single stone overlapping from one wall to another.
# {{lb|en|philately}} A cover having a stamp where the postmark cancellation overlaps the stamp.

